{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conway s law conway s law","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","fileName":"Conway's Law.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conway's Law","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Scaling Agile Teams]] [[Bounded Context and Organizational Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scaling Agile Teams","Bounded Context and Organizational Design","Bounded Context","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conway s law conway s law","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","fileName":"Conway's Law.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conway's Law","heading":"Conway's Law","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Conway's Law observes that a system's design tends to reproduce the communication structure of the organization that creates it. Teams separated by technology, discipline, or feature area often produce corresponding seams in the product.\n\nOrganizational design is therefore also product design. Cross-discipline feature teams and shared whole-game goals can reduce fragmentation that a component-centered hierarchy would otherwise embed.\n\nIn a domain-centered organization, teams divided by technical layer tend to produce matching seams and coordination queues. Cross-functional teams aligned to business capabilities can instead own one or more [[Bounded Context]]s. A context should not be split across multiple owners when that would require continuous agreement about its internal model.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scaling Agile Teams","Bounded Context and Organizational Design","Bounded Context","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conway s law conway s law","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conway's Law.md","fileName":"Conway's Law.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conway's Law","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]\n[[hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scaling Agile Teams","Bounded Context and Organizational Design","Bounded Context","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}